Task: Build the Docker image and run the full stack via docker compose up

Summary:
Built order-service:latest via sbt Docker/publishLocal (sbt-native-packager,
JavaAppPackaging + DockerPlugin), then ran it as a real container on the
docker-compose network (POSTGRES_HOST=postgres, port 8080 mapped) alongside a
freshly-started, real Postgres - not sbt run this time, the actual packaged
artifact. Exercised the full CRUD + health surface against the container:
POST/GET/PATCH/DELETE /orders, GET-after-DELETE (404), /health, /health/ready,
and Swagger UI at /docs - all passed.

docker-compose.yml itself stays Postgres-only per this track's Phase 1
decision; "the full stack" here means docker compose (Postgres) + the built
image run alongside it on the same Docker network, not adding order-service
as a compose service (which was never required by spec.md's FRs - only a
Docker image via sbt-native-packager was).

Files changed:
- scripts/verify-docker-image.sh (new)

Why: Closes this track's acceptance criteria - proves the Docker image (not
just the sbt-run dev path) is a real, deployable artifact.

Verification: the script itself is the verification - all 8 checks passed
(image built, Postgres healthy, container ready, POST/GET/PATCH/DELETE/health/
ready/docs all correct) against a real container instance.
